dist/index.js and dist/cleanup.js are single-file @vercel/ncc bundles: the whole
runtime dependency tree is inlined into them with no package boundaries, so this
list is the only human-readable inventory of what a consumer executes. An
earlier revision named two packages while the bundle in fact carried a full HTTP
stack; the entries below are the resolved runtime tree (`npm ls --omit=dev`)
cross-checked against strings present in the built bundle.

  @4cloudguru/terraform-drift-contract  Apache-2.0
  @4cloudguru/pipeline-task-core        Apache-2.0
  @actions/core                         MIT
  @actions/exec                         MIT
  @actions/http-client                  MIT
  @actions/io                           MIT
  tunnel                                MIT
  undici                                MIT
    includes formdata-polyfill          MIT  (vendored by undici; its banner
                                             appears verbatim in dist/index.js)

A machine-readable CycloneDX SBOM is generated at release time and attached to
each GitHub Release, alongside a build-provenance attestation over dist/index.js.
